# Agentforce Lightning Types — Architecture

A **Lightning Type** is a custom UI card that renders inside an Agentforce agent conversation window. Instead of the agent responding with plain text, it surfaces a rich interactive component — a calendar, menu, seat selector, image carousel, etc.

The card is triggered by an agent action (a Flow), returns a typed Apex payload, and the Lightning Type framework renders the associated LWC in the chat.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
User message
        │
        ▼
Agentforce Agent (Topic)
        │  calls
        ▼
AutoLaunchedFlow
        │  returns Apex object
        ▼
MyCardOutput (Apex payload class)
        │  matched by
        ▼
LightningTypeBundle: myCardType
  ├── schema.json         ← registers the Apex class as a Lightning Type
  └── renderer.json       ← maps to the LWC component
        │  renders
        ▼
LWC: myCardCmp            ← the actual UI in the chat window
        │  user interacts
        ▼
lightning__interaction event ← sends structured payload back to the agent
```

---

## File Structure

```
force-app/main/default/
│
├── classes/
│   ├── MyCardOutput.cls               ← Apex payload class (data contract)
│   └── MyCardOutput.cls-meta.xml
│
├── lightningTypes/
│   └── myCardType/
│       ├── schema.json                ← registers type, links to Apex class
│       └── lightningDesktopGenAi/
│           └── renderer.json          ← maps to LWC component
│
├── lwc/
│   └── myCardCmp/
│       ├── myCardCmp.html
│       ├── myCardCmp.js
│       ├── myCardCmp.css
│       └── myCardCmp.js-meta.xml
│
└── flows/
    └── My_Card_Flow.flow-meta.xml     ← AutoLaunchedFlow, invoked by agent action
```

---

## Every File — Correct Pattern

### 1. Apex Payload Class

```java
public class MyCardOutput {
    @AuraEnabled @InvocableVariable(label='Type' description='...') public String type;
    @AuraEnabled @InvocableVariable(label='Message' description='...') public String message;
}
```

- Must be `public` — NOT `global` (global breaks the Agentforce type binding)
- Every field needs BOTH `@AuraEnabled` AND `@InvocableVariable`
- Keep fields simple types: `String`, `Integer`, `Boolean`, `Decimal` — no `List<Object>`

---

### 2. `schema.json`

```json
{
  "title" : "My Card",
  "description" : "...",
  "lightning:type" : "@apexClassType/c__MyCardOutput"
}
```

- `lightning:type` format: `@apexClassType/c__<ClassName>`
- `c__` prefix = default namespace (no managed package)

---

### 3. `renderer.json`

```json
{
  "renderer" : {
    "componentOverrides" : {
      "$" : {
        "definition" : "c/myCardCmp"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

- Lives in the `lightningDesktopGenAi/` subfolder
- Component name uses `c/` prefix (default namespace), camelCase
- Do NOT add an `"attributes"` block — the framework passes the Apex payload to the LWC automatically as `@api value`

---

### 4. `js-meta.xml`

```xml
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>64.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__AgentforceOutput</target>
        <target>lightning__AppPage</target>
        <target>lightning__RecordPage</target>
        <target>lightning__HomePage</target>
    </targets>
</LightningComponentBundle>
```

- `lightning__AgentforceOutput` is required for the component to appear in Agentforce chat
- Do NOT add a `<targetConfigs>` block — this breaks rendering

---

### 5. LWC JS — receiving data and sending events

**Receiving the Apex payload:**
```js
import { LightningElement, api } from 'lwc';

export default class MyCardCmp extends LightningElement {
    @api value;   // Agentforce automatically passes the Apex object here

    get cardData() {
        return this.value || {};   // always guard against null
    }
}
```

**Sending data back to the agent:**
```js
this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('lightning__interaction', {
    bubbles: true,
    composed: true,
    detail: {
        interactionType: 'response',
        payload: {
            action: 'user_selection',
            message: 'User selected item X'
        }
    }
}));
```

- Use `lightning__interaction` — NOT `sendmessage`
- `interactionType` must be `'response'`
- Put whatever data you want the agent to act on in `payload`

---

### 6. Flow

```xml
<processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>

<!-- Output variable: the Apex payload object -->
<variables>
    <name>cardOutput</name>
    <apexClass>MyCardOutput</apexClass>
    <dataType>Apex</dataType>
    <isInput>false</isInput>
    <isOutput>true</isOutput>
</variables>

<!-- Input variable: required by Agentforce action UI (even if unused) -->
<variables>
    <name>userContext</name>
    <dataType>String</dataType>
    <isInput>true</isInput>
    <isOutput>false</isOutput>
</variables>
```

- Must be `AutoLaunchedFlow`
- You MUST have at least one input variable — the Agentforce action UI requires it

