## Agent Builder UI Setup

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Action Type | Flow |
| Output — Show in conversation | ✅ checked |
| Output — Output Rendering | set to your Lightning Type name |

---

## Common Mistakes

| # | Mistake | Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Apex class was `global` | Card rendered as plain text | Change to `public class` |
| 2 | Apex fields missing `@InvocableVariable` | Flow couldn't bind fields | Add `@InvocableVariable` to every field |
| 3 | `js-meta.xml` had `<targetConfigs>` | Component didn't render in chat | Remove `targetConfigs` entirely |
| 4 | `renderer.json` had `"attributes"` block | Value not passed to LWC | Remove the `attributes` block |
| 5 | LWC dispatched `sendmessage` event | Agent received raw text string | Change to `lightning__interaction` with `interactionType: 'response'` |
| 6 | Flow had no input variable | Agentforce action UI blocked | Add dummy `userContext` String input variable |
| 7 | Apex class used `List<Object>` property | LightningTypeBundle deploy failed | Use JSON `String` instead; parse in LWC |

---

## Checklist — Every New Lightning Type

- [ ] Apex: `public class`, `@AuraEnabled` + `@InvocableVariable` on every field, no `List<Object>`
- [ ] `schema.json`: `"lightning:type": "@apexClassType/c__<ClassName>"`
- [ ] `renderer.json`: just `"definition": "c/<lwcName>"` — no `attributes` block
- [ ] `js-meta.xml`: `lightning__AgentforceOutput` target, NO `targetConfigs`
- [ ] LWC JS: `@api value` to receive payload, `lightning__interaction` to respond
- [ ] Flow: `AutoLaunchedFlow`, Apex output variable, at least one String input variable
- [ ] Agent Builder: `Show in conversation` checked, `Output Rendering` set
- [ ] Agent version activated + Embedded Service Deployment re-published
